### 4.1 The four failures in detail

Descriptive; added at P3 before the second fact-check: no new run, no change of a pre-registered number, criterion or verdict. The numbers are generated by `report_scripts/bw_failures.py` (CSVs in `results/t3_r1/analysis/bw_failures/`). The best-response effort, the one-step argmax effort and the Beta spread are not in the analysis tables: they come from re-evaluating the stored last-iterate weights of the 40 `bw` runs with the evaluator of the round (final tier, pure), and that re-evaluation reproduces the stored arrays (mean effort, one-step gain and dynamic gain at every node of every stage) and the per-run scalars of all 40 runs bit for bit (`results/t3_r1/analysis/bw_failures/replay_check.json`). "Best-response effort" is the effort the verifier's dynamic best response plays at that stage and gap; "one-step argmax effort" is the argmax of the one-step deviation search (the two coincide at stage 3). `Delta_t(d)` is the one-step gain and `G_t(d)` the dynamic gain, both divided by dW; the normalised Beta sd is std(e)/(e_max - e_min) of the policy's Beta distribution at the gap.

**The failure: gate, part, value and limit, and the other gates** (**FAIL** marks the failing part; a run passes only if G-A, G-F and G-N all pass):

{{t17a_failure_gates}}

**Where the maximum is, and the policy there.** The failing quantity is `eta_3` (the first part of G-A) for the two q = 50 runs, at the gap of the stage-3 maximum of `Delta_3`, and `Gmax_full` (G-F) for the two q = 60 runs, at the gap of its maximum. All four gaps are in band (the stage-3 band is |d| < 4q = 200 at q = 50, the stage-2 band |d| < 2q = 120 at q = 60). At stage 3 the one-step and the dynamic gain coincide; at stage 2 the dynamic gain exceeds the one-step gain by 0.00027 (seed 50514) and 0.00016 (seed 50517) of dW, so almost the whole stage-2 gain at the maximum is the one-step gain.

{{t17b_failure_point}}

**The learned effort against the best response over d +- 20.** The figure shows every node of the window (step 2) for the failing run (the other 19 runs of the q in grey); the table shows every second node (step 4).

![learned effort against the best response, the four failing runs](../../../results/t3_r1/analysis/figures/bw_failures_windows.png)

{{t17c_failure_windows}}

**The training history of the failing stage's phase.** `Delta` is eta_t/dW of the development check of the phase (every 25 local updates, 64 checks; the learning rate decays linearly over local updates 1201-1600). It is the stage's own one-step gain with the later stages frozen; the G-F limit of 0.01 applies to `Gmax_full`, not to `Delta`, and the G-A limit of 0.005 to `eta_3`, which is `Delta` of the stage-3 phase.

