{{t17e_failure_rank}}

{{t17i_failing_quantity_top5}}

**The other 18 runs of the q at the same stage and gap.** The summary compares each failing run with the minimum, the median and the maximum of the other 18 runs of the q (the other failing run of the q excluded) at the failing stage and gap; the two full tables for q = 60 follow (all 20 runs at d = -14 and at d = -66, stage 2).

{{t17f_same_d_summary}}

**q = 60, stage 2, d = -14** (the gap of seed 50514's maximum):

{{t17g_same_d_q60_seed50514}}

**q = 60, stage 2, d = -66** (the gap of seed 50517's maximum):

{{t17g_same_d_q60_seed50517}}

**Stretches of near-zero effort inside the stage-2 band** (the nodes with |d| < 2q at which the learned mean effort is below 1, of an effort range of 100; all runs of the q that have any):

{{t17h_zero_effort_stage2}}

**What the data show** (descriptive; they do not say why):

- **q = 60, seeds 50514 and 50517 (G-F, stage 2): a stretch of near-zero effort inside the band, ending at the failing gap.** At the failing gap the learned mean effort is 0.52 (seed 50514, d = -14) and 0.16 (seed 50517, d = -66) where the best-response effort is 34.44 and 14.71, and the normalised Beta sd there is 0.0049 and 0.0024, against medians of 0.0162 and 0.0104 over their stage-2 grids. In the window the mean effort is 0.00 at d = -34 to -18 (seed 50514) and at most 0.01 at d = -86 to -70 (seed 50517) while the best response rises smoothly from 26.55 to 33.21 and from 9.85 to 13.63. In the stage-2 band the nodes with mean effort below 1 are 17 of 119 (d from -46 to -14; seed 50514) and 28 of 119 (d from -118 to -64; seed 50517); the maximum of `Delta_2` is at the inner end of the stretch (d = -14 is its last node for seed 50514; d = -66 is the node before its last node, d = -64, for seed 50517).
- **At q = 60 the failure is local to the run.** At d = -14 the other 18 runs have mean effort from 30.91 to 35.15 against best responses from 32.00 to 34.00, and `G_2(d)/dW` from 0.00015 to 0.00062; at d = -66, 12.09 to 14.61 against 12.69 to 14.51, and 0.00011 to 0.00044. The other failing run of the q lies inside these ranges at each of the two gaps (`G_2(d)/dW` 0.00040 at d = -14 and 0.00015 at d = -66). A stretch of near-zero effort in band is not unique to the two failing runs: seed 50519 has one (d from -118 to -82, 19 nodes) with a largest `Delta_2` of 0.00512, and it passes G-F (`G_max,2/dW` 0.00530); at q = 50 four runs have such a stretch at stage 2 (largest `Delta_2` 0.00089 to 0.00247).
- **q = 50, seeds 50504 and 50517 (G-A, `eta_3`, stage 3): no stretch of near-zero effort in the window; the policy is smooth and misses the best response by a margin that is largest near the maximum.** Seed 50504 plays 59.15 at d = -4 against a best response of 67.14: it is below the best response at every node of the window from d = -20 to d = +16 (by 1.79 to 11.77, largest at d = -12) and above it, by 2.03 and 0.25, at d = -24 and d = -22. Seed 50517 plays 64.29 at d = -18 against 48.02: it is above the best response at every node of the window from d = -38 to d = -2 (by 2.17 to 16.28, largest at d = -18) and within 0.34 of it at d = 0 and d = +2 (the nodes of the window are the grid nodes of step 2, `windows.csv`; the table shows every second one). The other 18 runs at the same gap have `Delta_3` up to 0.00449 (d = -4) and up to 0.00202 (d = -18), below the limit.
- **Training history.** Seed 50504 (q = 50, stage-3 phase): `Delta` is above 0.005 at 63 of the 64 checks (smallest 0.00486 at local 1125) and between 0.00510 and 0.01182 over the last 10, so its final value (0.00623) is typical of its last stretch. Seed 50517 (q = 50): `Delta` is at or below 0.005 at 31 of the 64 checks and at 9 of the last 10; it rises from 0.00067 at local 1575 to 0.00556 at local 1600, so its final value is an upward excursion after nine consecutive checks at or below the limit (local 1375 to 1575); the mean of its last 10 checks (0.00181) is below the median of the 20 runs (0.00254; rank 19 of 20). Seed 50514 (q = 60, stage-2 phase): `Delta` is 0.00747, 0.00726 and 0.00551 at local 100, 200 and 400 (smallest 0.00476 at local 300), then 0.01611 at local 800, 0.06122 at local 1200 and 0.05505 to 0.05958 over the last 10 checks: the gain formed between local 400 and 1200, before the learning-rate decay, and it did not recover during the decay. Seed 50517 (q = 60): smallest `Delta` 0.00167 at local 700, then 0.00594 at local 1200, 0.00816 at local 1400 and 0.00787 to 0.01057 over the last 10 checks (7 of the last 10 are at or below 0.01).
- **Rank.** The failing value is the largest of the 20 for seed 50504 (`eta_3` 0.00623; the next is 0.00568) and for seed 50514 (`Gmax_full` 0.05628; the next is 0.01089), and the second largest for seed 50517 at both q. The third largest are 0.00449 at q = 50 (90 % of the limit 0.005) and 0.00530 at q = 60 (limit 0.01); the medians are 0.00200 and 0.00139. At q = 50 the two failures are the top of a continuous series; at q = 60 the largest value is 5.2 times the second.
- **Seed 50517 fails at both q**, by different gates (G-A's `eta_3` part at q = 50, G-F at q = 60) and at different stages and gaps; its initial weights and random streams depend on (q, seed) and differ between the two q, so these are two different runs.

**What the data do not show.** Why the stretches of near-zero effort arise or persist, why seeds 50504 and 50517 under- and overshoot at q = 50, what these runs did differently from the other 18 of their q, and whether a repeat with another seed would fail. The round tested none of these and tries no remedy.

## 5. The comparison: H1, H2, H3

The pre-registered criterion: the paired difference of `Gmax_full/dW` (final tier, last iterate), mean over the 20 seeds, with the percentile bootstrap interval of the pairing by (q, seed) (S = 20261016 for H1, H2, H3 at T = 3 and S = 20261017 for H1-T2 at T = 2; 10,000 resamples); a hypothesis is supported iff the upper end of the 95 % interval is below 0 at both q. No run failed, so no pair was dropped (dropped pairs: 0 in all 8 cells).

{{t05a2_verdicts}}

{{t05a_criterion}}

**The levels behind the differences** (added at P3; descriptive, nothing pre-registered changes). The mean and the median over the 20 seeds of the ex-ante gain EXP_root/dW (the best-response gain at the root) and of the full-domain gain Gmax_full/dW, per arm and q (final tier, last iterate), so that the two measures can be compared arm by arm (prediction P2, section 7). The paired differences of both measures are in the table above (Gmax_full) and in the EXP_root rows of the secondary table below.

{{t05e_levels_t3}}

Reading of the three hypotheses (each statement is about the arms as implemented, at the equal-policy-row budget, 20 seeds per q):

- **H1** (`bw` - `jt`): supported at both q. Mean `Gmax_full/dW` 0.00249 (`bw`) against 0.18303 (`jt`) at q = 50, a difference of -0.18054 [-0.23237, -0.13464]; 0.00476 against 0.10495 at q = 60, -0.10019 [-0.12522, -0.07612]. 20 of 20 seeds at q = 50 and 19 of 20 at q = 60 have the negative sign. The q = 60 mean of `bw` contains seed 50514 (0.05628); the median difference (-0.09221 [-0.11937, -0.06076]) is of the same size as the mean difference.
- **H2** (`bw` - `jt_es`): supported at both q: -0.01115 [-0.01306, -0.00937] at q = 50, -0.00896 [-0.01317, -0.00252] at q = 60; 20 and 19 of 20 negative. This is the smallest of the three differences and the least tight one: at q = 60 the 98.75 % interval (Bonferroni over four hypotheses; descriptive) is [-0.01385, -0.00003], its upper end barely below 0, and the mean is pulled up by seed 50514 (the median difference is -0.01141 [-0.01371, -0.00881]). The `jt_es` means (0.01365 and 0.01373) are above the G-F threshold of 0.01.
- **H3** (`jt_es` - `jt`): supported at both q: -0.16939 [-0.22104, -0.12330] at q = 50 and -0.09122 [-0.11459, -0.06952] at q = 60, 20 of 20 negative at both. Exploring starts reduce the mean full-domain gain of the joint scheme by a factor of 13.4 (q = 50) and 7.6 (q = 60); `jt_es` stays above `bw`.
- The ordering `bw` < `jt_es` < `jt` in the mean `Gmax_full` holds at both q. The gate counts of the three arms (G-A and G-F on the final tier, G-N on both tiers; the T = 2 arms are in `05_t2_comparison.md`):

{{t04a2_gates_all_t3}}

  `jt` and `jt_es` pass G-N in 20 of 20 runs but G-A in none; `jt_es` passes G-F in 4 of 20 at each q, `jt` in none. The three parts of G-A and of G-N, counted per arm (all five arms):

{{t15_gate_parts}}

**The decomposition H1 = H2 + H3** (added at P3; descriptive). Over the same pairs the mean paired differences add exactly: the mean of `bw` - `jt` is the mean of `bw` - `jt_es` plus the mean of `jt_es` - `jt`. H1 therefore splits into the part that the exploring starts close (H3) and the part that remains between `bw` and `jt_es` (H2):

{{t05d_decomposition}}

At q = 50 the exploring starts close 0.938 of the mean `bw` - `jt` difference and 0.062 remains between `jt_es` and `bw`; at q = 60 the shares are 0.911 and 0.089. All three pairs have n = 20 at both q, so the shares are on the full 20 pairs and the residual H2 + H3 - H1 is zero to rounding (8.3e-17 and 0). The shares are statements about the means of these arms as implemented and carry the D5 caveats: **capacity** (`bw` is three networks, the joint arms one) and **start density** (`jt_es` covers every bin at a lower density per bin than `bw`). H2 is therefore not a test of the backward order alone, and the share H2/H1 is not the share of the effect that is due to the order.

**The secondaries** (paired differences, same pairing and bootstrap; `a - b` as in the criterion table; not criteria; the T = 2 pair is in `05_t2_comparison.md`):

{{t05b_secondary_t3}}

Reading: the scalar secondaries order the arms like `Gmax_full` (`bw` smallest, `jt` largest) with two exceptions among the pre-registered statistics. (1) The root effort e_1(0): `bw` has the largest, 45.58 (q = 50) and 34.85 (q = 60), `jt` the smallest (43.65 and 32.81); the `bw` - `jt` difference is +1.93 [+0.60, +3.38] and +2.04 [+1.00, +3.18] (the interval excludes 0), the `bw` - `jt_es` difference does not (+0.40 [-0.95, +1.80] and +0.36 [-1.37, +1.96]); the report does not compare e_1(0) with a closed form because none is part of D6 at T = 3. (2) The stage-1 deviation gain `Delta_max,1` (eta_1): `jt_es` has the larger one (the H3 difference is +0.00056 [-0.00030, +0.00143] at q = 50 and +0.00082 [+0.00005, +0.00164] at q = 60, with 7 and 6 of 20 seeds negative), while `bw` has the smallest (section 6). The per-stage and per-band paired differences are in section 6.

## 6. Where the gains are: by stage and band

The band at stage t >= 2 is |d| < 2q(t - 1), the gaps the equilibrium path can reach (D6); a node exactly at |d| = 2q(t - 1) is out of band. Medians over the 20 seeds (final tier; the rows of `v20` and `jt2` are discussed in `05_t2_comparison.md`). The full-domain maxima `G_max,t`, in band / out of band:

{{t06a_stage_band_medians}}

The one-step maxima `Delta_max,t` (eta_t), in band / out of band:

{{t06c_delta_medians}}

The stage and band of each run's largest gain (`Gmax_full`):

{{t06b_argmax_location}}

The gap at which each maximum is attained (median over the seeds of the absolute value of d, and the range of d over the seeds):

{{t16c_argmax_gaps}}

- **`jt` (joint, root starts only):** the largest gain of every run, at both q, is at **stage 2 and out of band** (20 of 20 and 20 of 20), at the edge of the domain: the argmax gap of `G_max,2` is |d| = 200 (q = 50, all 20 runs) and |d| = 220 (q = 60, all 20 runs), that of `G_max,3` 400 and 440 (median). The medians are G_out,2 = 0.158 (q = 50) and 0.093 (q = 60) against G_in,2 = 0.022 and 0.027; at stage 3, G_out,3 = 0.046 and 0.042 against G_in,3 = 0.019 and 0.033. The in-band quantities are not zero either (about 0.02 to 0.03), and the root-path quantity EXP_root is 0.0096 and 0.0097 on average (median 0.0091 and 0.0096): the policy is far closer to equilibrium on the gaps its own play reaches than elsewhere.
- **`jt_es`:** the largest gain is in band at stage 2 or 3 in 17 of 20 (q = 50; one further run has it at stage 1) and 16 of 20 (q = 60) runs, and at stage 2 in 15 and 17 of 20. Out of band the stage-2 and stage-3 medians are 0.0057 and 0.0009 (q = 50), 0.0091 and 0.0028 (q = 60), against in-band 0.0110 and 0.0084, 0.0127 and 0.0094. Its remaining excess is mainly an in-band excess, which is a different kind of failure from `jt`'s.
- **`bw`:** the largest gain is in band in all 40 runs and at stage 3 in 36 of them (19 and 17 of 20); the out-of-band stage-3 gain is 0.00001 (q = 50) and 0.00000 (q = 60) (medians).
- The paired band differences confirm the same picture for H1: at stage 2 the `bw` - `jt` difference of the out-of-band gain G_out,2 is -0.18272 [-0.23438, -0.13703] (q = 50) and -0.10469 [-0.12840, -0.08287] (q = 60), of the in-band gain G_in,2 -0.02355 and -0.02680 (all intervals exclude 0). The per-stage and per-band paired differences of all three T = 3 hypotheses:

{{t05c_stage_band_t3}}

